A destroy that does not sweep the capability tables
leaves capabilities naming dead objects,
and they come back to life when the memory is rebuilt into the same type.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: dangling object capability

diff --git a/kernel/cap.c b/kernel/cap.c
--- a/kernel/cap.c
+++ b/kernel/cap.c
@@ -242,2 +242,3 @@
         LOOP_WALK(cap_revoke_range);
+        continue;
         bool dying = range_contains(base, size, v2p(o));
